  "question": "A rider who uses a wheelchair travels this weekend from 34 St-Herald Sq to Grand Central-42 St using only the services and free transfers shown on this map. Walking between stations joined on the map counts as a transfer, and the trip ends when a train arrives at Grand Central-42 St itself. They can only enter, leave or change trains at stations marked with the accessibility symbol. They want the fewest transfers and, among those trips, the fewest station stops. Which services do they ride, in order? If more than one service runs between the same two stations on a leg, any of them is accepted. Answer as a JSON list of route letters or numbers, for example [\"A\", \"7\"].",
